%N A398458 Decimal expansion of Sum_{k>=1} H(k) * AH(k) / k^3, where H(k) = A001008(k)/A002805(k) is the k-th harmonic number, and AH(k) = A058313(k)/A058312(k) is the k-th alternating harmonic (or skew-harmonic) number.
%H A398458 Cornel Ioan Vălean, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-031-21262-8">More (Almost) Impossible Integrals, Sums, and Series</a>, Springer Cham, 2023. See section 4.46, p. 439, eq. (4.145), section 5.46, p. 466, section 6.46, pp. 715-723.
%H A398458 <a href="/index/Ha#harmonic">Index entries for sequences related to harmonic numbers</a>.
